course: dictionary
lesson: 14748
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can do two different jobs. Pronounced is one of them. Read the sentence and ask: is this word describing something, or is it an action that has already happened? «He walked with a pronounced limp.» Here pronounced describes the limp. You can easily see the limp, so pronounced means very noticeable.
explain: «She pronounced the word well.» Now pronounced is an action. Pronounce means to say a word out loud, so pronounced is the past form, like said. Check by swapping in said: «She said the word well» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: The words next to pronounced give the clues. A limp, an accent or a change is something you notice, so pronounced means clear and strong. A word or a name is something you say, so pronounced means said out loud. Look at what comes after it.
fact: Pronounced is an adjective meaning very noticeable, strong or clear.
fact: «A pronounced limp» means a limp that you can see easily.
fact: «A pronounced accent» means an accent that is easy to hear.
fact: Pronounced is also the past form of pronounce, which means to say a word out loud.
fact: «More pronounced» means even clearer or stronger than before.
exercise: «The doctor noticed a pronounced limp in his left leg.» What does pronounced mean here? | Very quiet | Said out loud | *Very noticeable | Hidden
exercise: «The teacher pronounced the long word slowly.» What does pronounced mean here? | Very noticeable and strong | Written down | Forgotten | *Said out loud, the past of pronounce
exercise: «There was a pronounced change in the temperature overnight.» What does pronounced mean here? | *Big and clear | Small and hidden | Said out loud | Cold and wet
test: «The scientists saw a pronounced change in the temperature.» What does pronounced mean? | *Very clear and big | Said out loud | Hidden and small | Cold and wet
test: «Ben pronounced his name carefully for the new teacher.» What does pronounced mean here? | Forgot | Hid | *Said out loud | Very noticeable
exam: «The effect of the medicine was pronounced after one day.» What does pronounced mean here? | Said out loud | *Strong and easy to notice | Written down | Hard to see
